  "_comment": [
    "One fully populated Interaction, exactly as the Python SDK writes it.",
    "Every language decodes this, rebuilds the nested Chunk / Status /",
    "ActionMessage / NodeFragment / ActionConfig / Peer / UsageMetadata it",
    "contains, re-encodes, and must produce these bytes again. That is what",
    "makes a conversation held in one language safe to hand to another: the",
    "interaction a peer sends back has to be the one it received.",
    "Rebuild with GOLDEN_INTERACTION in a11/data/tests/test_serial_tags.py",
    "if the wire format changes on purpose -- and expect the other",
    "languages' tests to fail until they agree."
